.TH YUME-GUI 1 "May 2026" "yume" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
yume-gui \- desktop UI for the Yume post-quantum stealth transport
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B yume-gui
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B yume-gui
is an optional Dear ImGui-based desktop application. It embeds the
server facade for local
.BR yumed (8)
control and starts the real
.BR yume (1)
client runtime in the background, attaching to it through local IPC.
.PP
The GUI is a thin layer over the same transport stack used by
.BR yume (1)
and
.BR yumed (8).
Configuration files written by the GUI are compatible with the CLI.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --headless
Run a no-window smoke test of the embedded facade. Useful for verifying
the build on systems without a display server.
.TP
.B --start-minimized
Open the application hidden. The system tray icon (if present) can be
used to show the window.
.TP
.B --no-tray
Disable the system tray icon at runtime. Equivalent to a build without
tray support.
.TP
.BI --client-config " path"
Load the client configuration from
.IR path
instead of the platform default.
.TP
.BI --server-config " path"
Load the server configuration from
.IR path
instead of the platform default.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print a help summary and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.yume/client.json
Default GUI client profile.
.TP
.I ~/.yume/server.json
Default GUI server configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.yume/secure-materials/
Trusted anonym CAs and imported client auth keys.
.TP
.I ~/.yume/keys/
Default key generation directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR yume (1),
.BR yumed (8)
.SH AUTHOR
FixCraft Inc.
